      "copy": [
        "From “ARGH, WTF?” to “Ah. That’s why.”",
        "From “OMG, the end is nigh!” to “Ugh, as if.”",
        "From “Whatever” to “RSVP: Yes. I have notes!”"
      ],
      "cards": [
        {
          "rect": {
            "x": 40,
            "y": 538.578125,
            "width": 310,
            "height": 417.84375,
            "right": 350,
            "bottom": 956.421875
          },
          "text": "Use it better. Take your career further.From “ARGH, WTF?” to “Ah. That’s why.”What you ask, what context you provide, what the system can see and how you evaluate its answer can all change the result. Understand why an AI tool has gone off track—and what you can do about it. These are practical career skills: strengthening your work, exercising judgment and preparing for new responsibilities."
        },
        {
          "rect": {
            "x": 40,
            "y": 972.421875,
            "width": 310,
            "height": 467.921875,
            "right": 350,
            "bottom": 1440.34375
          },
          "text": "See through the noise. Make sound decisions.From “OMG, the end is nigh!” to “Ugh, as if.”You cannot cut through that noise by memorising a list of approved opinions. You need enough of the fundamentals to ask: What evidence supports the claim? What does the demonstration leave out? What would have to be true for this prediction to happen? That is how you evaluate a tool, a workplace proposal or a headline on its merits."
        },
        {
          "rect": {
            "x": 40,
            "y": 1456.34375,
            "width": 310,
            "height": 443.609375,
            "right": 350,
            "bottom": 1899.953125
          },
          "text": "Have a say. Help change the defaults.From “Whatever” to “RSVP: Yes. I have notes!”Once you understand how AI works, you can participate meaningfully in decisions about what happens next. These debates are already happening—in workplaces, governments, schools, city halls and homes. Refusing to engage does not stop decisions from being made. It only means they will be made without you."
        }
